{
 "$comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later. Expected I/O worked out from OpenRGB's C++ (commit d4798c120659ec5ba2e664a9e87bedff8d36f880, Controllers/RoccatController: RoccatKoneAimoController, RoccatKoneProController, RoccatKoneProAirController, RoccatKoneXPController, RoccatBurstController, their RGBControllers and RoccatControllerDetect.cpp) by a separate reference model (openrgb-work/batch2/roccat/gen.py in the porting session's scratch space, not in the repository); plugin.js was never run to make them. Per variant: LED names and grid cells (zones in OpenRGB order, a multi-LED zone gets its own row, consecutive one-LED zones share a row), two colour sets in LED order, and the I/O of Initialize, a frame with each colour set and Shutdown. Deliberate Lightloom deviations (docs/hardware/roccat-mouse.md): Kone XP enters direct with EnableDirect(on) and one ready poll only (OpenRGB's profile write SetMode, which also carries DPI and polling rate, is never sent); Kone Pro, Burst and Kone XP Shutdown switch back to the built-in lighting (0E 06 01 00 00 FF); Kone Aimo keeps the 0D 2E header constant; Kone Aimo and Kone Pro Air Shutdown send black. ops: send_report = SET_FEATURE, get_report = GET_FEATURE (report id, length), write = output report. 'held_back' lists OpenRGB ids this plugin does not claim, with the reason.",
